{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["Because he places — before he blessed them, Yosef saw that his father had crossed his hands, and Yosef said to his father: Not so, my father. One should not explain this as Yosef saying 'you are not doing well' — for then he should have asked his father 'why are you doing this?' Rather, this is what Yosef said to Yaakov: 'The sons are not arranged as you suppose — you thought I had not been careful to bring them in order to your right and your left, to place the firstborn at your right and the younger at your left; rather, I took the firstborn at my right and the younger at my left. That is why you are bending your hands, bringing your hand to move it from the head of Ephraim in order to place it on the head of Menashe.' And so all forms of הסרה are written in the piel: סורה אלי אל תירא — turn from there toward me; ויסורו אליו — they turned from there to come to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {0 "Rashbam reads לא כן אבי not as a protest but as a factual correction: Yosef is telling Yaakov that he, Yosef, had in fact arranged the sons correctly by birth order. The clause להבאתי להסיר אותה is read as Yosef's explanation of why Yaakov is bending his hands; Rashbam then notes that the verb forms of ס-ו-ר cited as parallels are all in the piel binyan."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:47:37.168462980Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}